Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"Load resource index JSON": "Ressourcenindex als JSON laden", "Declared observation": "Deklarierte Beobachtung", "Source metadata": "Quellmetadaten", "Imported index; local files and native availability were not checked.": "Importierter Index; lokale Dateien und native Verfügbarkeit wurden nicht geprüft.", "Resource index loaded. Local files were not checked.": "Ressourcenindex geladen. Lokale Dateien wurden nicht geprüft.", "addons": "Addons", "Unresolved resource references": "Nicht aufgelöste Ressourcenreferenzen", "Showing up to 50": "Bis zu 50 angezeigt", "Load an exported resource index in Assets to review identities and declared dependency gaps. Imported file observations are not rechecked.": "Einen exportierten Index unter Ressourcen laden, um Identitäten und deklarierte Abhängigkeiten zu prüfen. Importierte Dateibeobachtungen werden nicht erneut geprüft."});

window.PlannerTranslations.fr["Assets → Import Workbench metadata → Select project and sidecars opens two native file pickers: choose addon.gproj, then up to 500 .meta files inside that project. The worker reads supported identities only. Review resource paths, GUIDs, empty/missing target warnings and dependency gaps; use the warning filter and pages. Export resource index saves the reviewed metadata. Use reviewed resource index makes it available in unit property review and invalidates any older property review. Neither action edits the mission or spawns game entities. Cancellation or rejected files retain the previous metadata review. Clear metadata review affects this panel only; clear the property source index separately if needed. Restart clears session metadata. Native loading, component configurations and server availability remain unverified. Expand a prefab row, choose Planning asset name and Planning asset type, then Prepare unit asset. In Units, Apply changes or Place new unit saves its GUID and provenance with that unit. Preparing alone does not edit the mission; unassigned catalog entries last only for this session. Review project identity only chooses just addon.gproj and lists its addon identity and declared dependency gaps, with zero prefab resources. GameProject Configurations blocks are accepted as opaque text. Download manifests cannot supply prefab GUIDs; use verified metadata sidecars for asset assignment. Load resource index JSON opens one native JSON picker for an exported Companion resource index, including multiple addons. Imported observations are declarations; referenced files and native availability are not checked. Review owner IDs and declared dependency gaps, then prepare GUID-qualified prefab assets normally. Cancelled or invalid indexes retain the previous review."]=window.PlannerTranslations.fr["Assets → Import Workbench metadata → Select project and sidecars opens two native file pickers: choose addon.gproj, then up to 500 .meta files inside that project. The worker reads supported identities only. Review resource paths, GUIDs, empty/missing target warnings and dependency gaps; use the warning filter and pages. Export resource index saves the reviewed metadata. Use reviewed resource index makes it available in unit property review and invalidates any older property review. Neither action edits the mission or spawns game entities. Cancellation or rejected files retain the previous metadata review. Clear metadata review affects this panel only; clear the property source index separately if needed. Restart clears session metadata. Native loading, component configurations and server availability remain unverified. Expand a prefab row, choose Planning asset name and Planning asset type, then Prepare unit asset. In Units, Apply changes or Place new unit saves its GUID and provenance with that unit. Preparing alone does not edit the mission; unassigned catalog entries last only for this session. Review project identity only chooses just addon.gproj and lists its addon identity and declared dependency gaps, with zero prefab resources. GameProject Configurations blocks are accepted as opaque text. Download manifests cannot supply prefab GUIDs; use verified metadata sidecars for asset assignment."]+" Charger un index de ressources JSON ouvre une sélection native pour un index Companion exporté, avec plusieurs addons possibles. Les observations importées sont déclaratives ; fichiers référencés et disponibilité native ne sont pas vérifiés. Vérifiez propriétaires et dépendances, puis préparez les prefabs avec GUID. Annulation ou index invalide conserve la vérification précédente.";

window.PlannerTranslations.de["Assets → Import Workbench metadata → Select project and sidecars opens two native file pickers: choose addon.gproj, then up to 500 .meta files inside that project. The worker reads supported identities only. Review resource paths, GUIDs, empty/missing target warnings and dependency gaps; use the warning filter and pages. Export resource index saves the reviewed metadata. Use reviewed resource index makes it available in unit property review and invalidates any older property review. Neither action edits the mission or spawns game entities. Cancellation or rejected files retain the previous metadata review. Clear metadata review affects this panel only; clear the property source index separately if needed. Restart clears session metadata. Native loading, component configurations and server availability remain unverified. Expand a prefab row, choose Planning asset name and Planning asset type, then Prepare unit asset. In Units, Apply changes or Place new unit saves its GUID and provenance with that unit. Preparing alone does not edit the mission; unassigned catalog entries last only for this session. Review project identity only chooses just addon.gproj and lists its addon identity and declared dependency gaps, with zero prefab resources. GameProject Configurations blocks are accepted as opaque text. Download manifests cannot supply prefab GUIDs; use verified metadata sidecars for asset assignment. Load resource index JSON opens one native JSON picker for an exported Companion resource index, including multiple addons. Imported observations are declarations; referenced files and native availability are not checked. Review owner IDs and declared dependency gaps, then prepare GUID-qualified prefab assets normally. Cancelled or invalid indexes retain the previous review."]=window.PlannerTranslations.de["Assets → Import Workbench metadata → Select project and sidecars opens two native file pickers: choose addon.gproj, then up to 500 .meta files inside that project. The worker reads supported identities only. Review resource paths, GUIDs, empty/missing target warnings and dependency gaps; use the warning filter and pages. Export resource index saves the reviewed metadata. Use reviewed resource index makes it available in unit property review and invalidates any older property review. Neither action edits the mission or spawns game entities. Cancellation or rejected files retain the previous metadata review. Clear metadata review affects this panel only; clear the property source index separately if needed. Restart clears session metadata. Native loading, component configurations and server availability remain unverified. Expand a prefab row, choose Planning asset name and Planning asset type, then Prepare unit asset. In Units, Apply changes or Place new unit saves its GUID and provenance with that unit. Preparing alone does not edit the mission; unassigned catalog entries last only for this session. Review project identity only chooses just addon.gproj and lists its addon identity and declared dependency gaps, with zero prefab resources. GameProject Configurations blocks are accepted as opaque text. Download manifests cannot supply prefab GUIDs; use verified metadata sidecars for asset assignment."]+" Ressourcenindex als JSON laden öffnet einen nativen Dialog für einen exportierten Companion-Index mit mehreren Addons. Importierte Beobachtungen sind Deklarationen; referenzierte Dateien und native Verfügbarkeit werden nicht geprüft. Eigentümer und Abhängigkeiten prüfen und dann Prefabs mit GUID vorbereiten. Abbruch oder ungültiger Index behält die vorherige Prüfung.";

window.PlannerTranslations.fr["In the dedicated SERVER’s resolved $profile folder, edit JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. With -profile A:/ServerTest, this is A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. Paste the ADDRESS into endpoint and the CODE into pairingCode. Set enabled to true and configure the authorised named entity. No game pause-menu pairing is needed."]="Dans le dossier $profile résolu du SERVEUR dédié, modifiez JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. Avec -profile A:/ServerTest, le fichier est A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. Collez l’ADRESSE dans endpoint et le CODE dans pairingCode. Activez enabled et configurez l’entité nommée autorisée. Aucun appairage dans le menu pause du jeu n’est requis.";

window.PlannerTranslations.de["In the dedicated SERVER’s resolved $profile folder, edit JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. With -profile A:/ServerTest, this is A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. Paste the ADDRESS into endpoint and the CODE into pairingCode. Set enabled to true and configure the authorised named entity. No game pause-menu pairing is needed."]="JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json im aufgelösten $profile-Ordner des dedizierten SERVERS bearbeiten. Mit -profile A:/ServerTest liegt sie unter A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. ADRESSE in endpoint und CODE in pairingCode einfügen, enabled aktivieren und die autorisierte benannte Entität konfigurieren. Keine Kopplung im Spiel-Pausemenü nötig.";

window.PlannerTranslations.fr["Open Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Choose Dedicated server, enter a profile name, and choose Free temporary tunnel or an existing HTTPS relay. Save profile stores settings without secrets. Connect profile creates a temporary pairing code and closes the previous connection. Give the displayed address and code to the server administrator for the private JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. The v2.9.1 addon candidate sends one named scenario entity only. It is experimental until tested on a real dedicated server; the published Host Local mod alone is insufficient. See DEDICATED-SERVER.md in the release. Place that config in the resolved $profile folder: -profile A:/ServerTest maps to A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. After disabling or revoking a sender, create a fresh pairing session before enabling it again."]=window.PlannerTranslations.fr["Open Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Choose Dedicated server, enter a profile name, and choose Free temporary tunnel or an existing HTTPS relay. Save profile stores settings without secrets. Connect profile creates a temporary pairing code and closes the previous connection. Give the displayed address and code to the server administrator for the private JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. The v2.9.1 addon candidate sends one named scenario entity only. It is experimental until tested on a real dedicated server; the published Host Local mod alone is insufficient. See DEDICATED-SERVER.md in the release."]+" Placez le fichier dans le dossier $profile résolu : -profile A:/ServerTest correspond à A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. Après désactivation ou révocation, créez une nouvelle session avant de réactiver.";

window.PlannerTranslations.de["Open Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Choose Dedicated server, enter a profile name, and choose Free temporary tunnel or an existing HTTPS relay. Save profile stores settings without secrets. Connect profile creates a temporary pairing code and closes the previous connection. Give the displayed address and code to the server administrator for the private JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. The v2.9.1 addon candidate sends one named scenario entity only. It is experimental until tested on a real dedicated server; the published Host Local mod alone is insufficient. See DEDICATED-SERVER.md in the release. Place that config in the resolved $profile folder: -profile A:/ServerTest maps to A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. After disabling or revoking a sender, create a fresh pairing session before enabling it again."]=window.PlannerTranslations.de["Open Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Choose Dedicated server, enter a profile name, and choose Free temporary tunnel or an existing HTTPS relay. Save profile stores settings without secrets. Connect profile creates a temporary pairing code and closes the previous connection. Give the displayed address and code to the server administrator for the private JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. The v2.9.1 addon candidate sends one named scenario entity only. It is experimental until tested on a real dedicated server; the published Host Local mod alone is insufficient. See DEDICATED-SERVER.md in the release."]+" Konfiguration im aufgelösten $profile-Ordner ablegen: -profile A:/ServerTest entspricht A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. Nach Deaktivierung oder Widerruf vor erneutem Aktivieren eine neue Kopplung erstellen.";

window.PlannerTranslations.fr["Open Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Choose Dedicated server, enter a profile name, and choose Free temporary tunnel or an existing HTTPS relay. Save profile stores settings without secrets. Connect profile creates a temporary pairing code and closes the previous connection. Give the displayed address and code to the server administrator for the private JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. The v2.9.1 addon candidate sends one named scenario entity only. It remains experimental. A bounded standalone server HTTPS position test passed; the older published Host Local mod alone is insufficient. See DEDICATED-SERVER.md in the release. Place that config in the resolved $profile folder: -profile A:/ServerTest maps to A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. After disabling or revoking a sender, create a fresh pairing session before enabling it again."]="Ouvrez Paramètres → Pont en direct → Profils serveur / Serveur dédié. Choisissez Serveur dédié, un nom et un tunnel temporaire gratuit ou relais HTTPS existant. Enregistrez le profil puis connectez-le pour obtenir une nouvelle adresse et un code temporaire. Transmettez-les à l’administrateur pour JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. Le module v2.9.1 transmet une seule entité nommée autorisée. Un test HTTPS limité sur serveur dédié autonome a réussi ; les scénarios complets restent expérimentaux et l’ancien module Host Local ne suffit pas. Consultez DEDICATED-SERVER.md. Avec -profile A:/ServerTest, placez le fichier dans A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. Après désactivation ou révocation, créez une nouvelle session avant de réactiver.";

window.PlannerTranslations.fr["A bounded standalone dedicated-server HTTPS test passed; full scenarios remain experimental."]="Un test HTTPS limité sur serveur dédié autonome a réussi ; les scénarios complets restent expérimentaux.";

window.PlannerTranslations.de["Open Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Choose Dedicated server, enter a profile name, and choose Free temporary tunnel or an existing HTTPS relay. Save profile stores settings without secrets. Connect profile creates a temporary pairing code and closes the previous connection. Give the displayed address and code to the server administrator for the private JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. The v2.9.1 addon candidate sends one named scenario entity only. It remains experimental. A bounded standalone server HTTPS position test passed; the older published Host Local mod alone is insufficient. See DEDICATED-SERVER.md in the release. Place that config in the resolved $profile folder: -profile A:/ServerTest maps to A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. After disabling or revoking a sender, create a fresh pairing session before enabling it again."]="Einstellungen → Live-Brücke → Serverprofile / Dedizierter Server öffnen. Dedizierter Server, Profilname und kostenlosen temporären Tunnel oder vorhandenen HTTPS-Relay wählen. Profil speichern und verbinden, um Adresse und temporären Code zu erhalten. Beides dem Administrator für JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json geben. Das v2.9.1-Addon überträgt nur eine ausdrücklich autorisierte benannte Entität. Ein begrenzter HTTPS-Test auf einem eigenständigen dedizierten Server ist bestanden; vollständige Szenarien bleiben experimentell und das ältere Host-Local-Addon reicht nicht aus. DEDICATED-SERVER.md beachten. Mit -profile A:/ServerTest liegt die Datei unter A:/ServerTest/profile/JSOC_ORBAT_Dedicated.json. Nach Deaktivierung oder Widerruf vor erneutem Aktivieren eine neue Kopplung erstellen.";

window.PlannerTranslations.de["A bounded standalone dedicated-server HTTPS test passed; full scenarios remain experimental."]="Ein begrenzter HTTPS-Test auf einem eigenständigen dedizierten Server ist bestanden; vollständige Szenarien bleiben experimentell.";

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"Tracking scope": "Périmètre du suivi", "One authorised entity": "Une entité autorisée", "Named entity allowlist — up to 60 (experimental)": "Liste explicite — jusqu’à 60 entités (expérimental)", "Tracked entity IDs — one per line": "Identifiants suivis — un par ligne", "Allowlist tracking requires the new tracked sender and protocol 3 relay. Workshop 0.2.0 supports single-entity tracking. No automatic connection at startup.": "Le suivi par liste nécessite le nouveau module et le relais protocole 3. Workshop 0.2.0 suit une seule entité. Aucune connexion automatique au démarrage.", "Open Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Choose Dedicated server and Named entity allowlist — up to 60 (experimental). Enter one tracked ID per line and use a 1–2 second interval. Save profile excludes credentials. Connect profile creates temporary pairing. The administrator puts the address, code and matching entityNames/entityIds into private JSOC_ORBAT_Tracked.json in the resolved server profile folder. The tracking pilot addon and protocol 3 relay are required; Workshop 0.2.0 supports single-entity tracking. A real standalone HTTPS test passed for 60 synthetic entities, movement, stationary heartbeats and removal. Live markers remain separate from the saved plan. No automatic player discovery. See TRACKED-ENTITIES-PILOT.md. Stop revokes the session; reconnect with a fresh code.": "Ouvrez Paramètres → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Choisissez Dedicated server et la liste explicite de 60 entités maximum. Saisissez un identifiant par ligne et un intervalle de 1–2 secondes. Save profile exclut les codes. Connect profile crée un code temporaire. L’administrateur renseigne endpoint, pairingCode et les paires entityNames/entityIds dans le fichier privé JSOC_ORBAT_Tracked.json du profil serveur. Le module tracking pilot et un relais protocole 3 sont requis ; Workshop 0.2.0 suit une seule entité. Le test HTTPS réel a validé 60 entités synthétiques, déplacement, présence stationnaire et suppression. Les marqueurs ne modifient pas le plan. Aucune découverte automatique des joueurs. Consultez TRACKED-ENTITIES-PILOT.md. Stop révoque la session ; utilisez un nouveau code pour reconnecter."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"Tracking scope": "Tracking-Umfang", "One authorised entity": "Eine autorisierte Entität", "Named entity allowlist — up to 60 (experimental)": "Explizite Liste — bis zu 60 Entitäten (experimentell)", "Tracked entity IDs — one per line": "Verfolgte Entitäts-IDs — eine pro Zeile", "Allowlist tracking requires the new tracked sender and protocol 3 relay. Workshop 0.2.0 supports single-entity tracking. No automatic connection at startup.": "Listen-Tracking benötigt das neue Modul und einen Protokoll-3-Relay. Workshop 0.2.0 verfolgt eine Entität. Keine automatische Verbindung beim Start.", "Open Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Choose Dedicated server and Named entity allowlist — up to 60 (experimental). Enter one tracked ID per line and use a 1–2 second interval. Save profile excludes credentials. Connect profile creates temporary pairing. The administrator puts the address, code and matching entityNames/entityIds into private JSOC_ORBAT_Tracked.json in the resolved server profile folder. The tracking pilot addon and protocol 3 relay are required; Workshop 0.2.0 supports single-entity tracking. A real standalone HTTPS test passed for 60 synthetic entities, movement, stationary heartbeats and removal. Live markers remain separate from the saved plan. No automatic player discovery. See TRACKED-ENTITIES-PILOT.md. Stop revokes the session; reconnect with a fresh code.": "Öffnen Sie Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles / Dedicated server. Wählen Sie Dedicated server und die explizite Liste mit höchstens 60 Entitäten. Geben Sie eine ID pro Zeile und ein Intervall von 1–2 Sekunden ein. Save profile speichert keine Zugangsdaten. Connect profile erstellt einen temporären Code. Der Administrator trägt endpoint, pairingCode und passende entityNames/entityIds in die private JSOC_ORBAT_Tracked.json im Serverprofil ein. Tracking-Pilot-Modul und Protokoll-3-Relay sind erforderlich; Workshop 0.2.0 verfolgt eine Entität. Der echte HTTPS-Test bestätigte 60 synthetische Entitäten, Bewegung, stationäre Meldungen und Entfernung. Marker ändern den gespeicherten Plan nicht. Keine automatische Spielererkennung. Siehe TRACKED-ENTITIES-PILOT.md. Stop widerruft die Sitzung; danach neuen Code verwenden."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"Deployment preview": "Aperçu du déploiement", "Review 1–16 selected units with verified prefab references. Exports intentions only; nothing is spawned in the game.": "Examinez 1–16 unités sélectionnées avec références prefab vérifiées. Export des intentions uniquement ; aucune création dans le jeu.", "Load deployment resource index": "Charger l’index de déploiement", "Clear deployment review": "Effacer l’aperçu de déploiement", "No deployment resource index": "Aucun index de déploiement", "Deployment heading (degrees)": "Orientation du déploiement (degrés)", "Review selected units": "Examiner les unités sélectionnées", "Export reviewed deployment JSON": "Exporter le JSON de déploiement examiné", "No deployment review": "Aucun aperçu de déploiement", "Plan or heading changed. Review deployment again.": "Plan ou orientation modifiés. Examinez à nouveau le déploiement.", "Deployment reviewed. Native validation is still required.": "Déploiement examiné. La validation native reste requise.", "Required addons": "Modules requis", "Unresolved addon metadata": "Métadonnées de modules manquantes", "Terrain elevation must be resolved by the server.": "L’altitude du terrain doit être résolue par le serveur.", "Deployment resource index loaded": "Index de déploiement chargé", "Load a resource index before reviewing deployment.": "Chargez un index avant d’examiner le déploiement.", "Deployment review rejected": "Aperçu de déploiement refusé", "Deployment export requested. Check your downloads.": "Export de déploiement demandé. Vérifiez vos téléchargements.", "Deployment export rejected": "Export de déploiement refusé", "Open deployment preview": "Ouvrir l’aperçu de déploiement", "Deployment preview reviews selected units without changing the mission or sending game commands.": "L’aperçu examine les unités sélectionnées sans modifier la mission ni envoyer de commandes au jeu.", "In Units, select 1–16 units with reviewed prefab assets. Open Deployment preview, load the matching resource index, set a heading and click Review selected units. Check positions, GUID provenance and required addons. Export reviewed deployment JSON opens a Save dialog for an intention package; it does not spawn anything. Changes to the plan, heading or source index require a new review. Missing addon metadata is shown explicitly. The server must validate native resources and terrain elevation before any future execution. Settings → Deployment preview opens this panel. See DEPLOYMENT-INTENT-PILOT.md.": "Dans Units, sélectionnez 1–16 unités avec des prefabs examinés. Ouvrez l’aperçu de déploiement, chargez l’index correspondant, réglez l’orientation et examinez les unités. Vérifiez positions, provenance GUID et modules requis. L’export JSON contient des intentions ; aucune unité n’est créée. Toute modification du plan, de l’orientation ou de l’index impose une nouvelle vérification. Les métadonnées manquantes sont indiquées. Le serveur doit vérifier les ressources natives et l’altitude avant une future exécution. Paramètres → Aperçu du déploiement ouvre le panneau. Consultez DEPLOYMENT-INTENT-PILOT.md."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"Deployment preview": "Bereitstellungsvorschau", "Review 1–16 selected units with verified prefab references. Exports intentions only; nothing is spawned in the game.": "Prüfen Sie 1–16 ausgewählte Einheiten mit geprüften Prefab-Referenzen. Nur Absichten werden exportiert; im Spiel wird nichts erzeugt.", "Load deployment resource index": "Bereitstellungs-Ressourcenindex laden", "Clear deployment review": "Bereitstellungsprüfung löschen", "No deployment resource index": "Kein Bereitstellungs-Ressourcenindex", "Deployment heading (degrees)": "Bereitstellungsrichtung (Grad)", "Review selected units": "Ausgewählte Einheiten prüfen", "Export reviewed deployment JSON": "Geprüfte Bereitstellung als JSON exportieren", "No deployment review": "Keine Bereitstellungsprüfung", "Plan or heading changed. Review deployment again.": "Plan oder Richtung geändert. Bereitstellung erneut prüfen.", "Deployment reviewed. Native validation is still required.": "Bereitstellung geprüft. Native Validierung bleibt erforderlich.", "Required addons": "Erforderliche Addons", "Unresolved addon metadata": "Fehlende Addon-Metadaten", "Terrain elevation must be resolved by the server.": "Die Geländehöhe muss vom Server ermittelt werden.", "Deployment resource index loaded": "Bereitstellungs-Ressourcenindex geladen", "Load a resource index before reviewing deployment.": "Vor der Bereitstellungsprüfung einen Ressourcenindex laden.", "Deployment review rejected": "Bereitstellungsprüfung abgelehnt", "Deployment export requested. Check your downloads.": "Bereitstellungsexport angefordert. Downloads prüfen.", "Deployment export rejected": "Bereitstellungsexport abgelehnt", "Open deployment preview": "Bereitstellungsvorschau öffnen", "Deployment preview reviews selected units without changing the mission or sending game commands.": "Die Vorschau prüft ausgewählte Einheiten, ohne die Mission zu ändern oder Spielbefehle zu senden.", "In Units, select 1–16 units with reviewed prefab assets. Open Deployment preview, load the matching resource index, set a heading and click Review selected units. Check positions, GUID provenance and required addons. Export reviewed deployment JSON opens a Save dialog for an intention package; it does not spawn anything. Changes to the plan, heading or source index require a new review. Missing addon metadata is shown explicitly. The server must validate native resources and terrain elevation before any future execution. Settings → Deployment preview opens this panel. See DEPLOYMENT-INTENT-PILOT.md.": "Wählen Sie unter Units 1–16 Einheiten mit geprüften Prefabs. Öffnen Sie die Bereitstellungsvorschau, laden Sie den passenden Ressourcenindex und prüfen Sie die Einheiten mit der gewünschten Richtung. Prüfen Sie Positionen, GUID-Herkunft und benötigte Addons. Der JSON-Export enthält nur Absichten und erzeugt keine Einheiten. Änderungen an Plan, Richtung oder Index erfordern eine neue Prüfung. Fehlende Metadaten werden angezeigt. Vor einer späteren Ausführung muss der Server native Ressourcen und Geländehöhe prüfen. Settings → Bereitstellungsvorschau öffnet das Panel. Siehe DEPLOYMENT-INTENT-PILOT.md."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"Deployment JSON saved.": "JSON de déploiement enregistré.", "Deployment export cancelled.": "Export de déploiement annulé.", "Deployment export requires the desktop application.": "L’export nécessite l’application de bureau."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"Deployment JSON saved.": "Bereitstellungs-JSON gespeichert.", "Deployment export cancelled.": "Bereitstellungsexport abgebrochen.", "Deployment export requires the desktop application.": "Der Export benötigt die Desktop-Anwendung."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"Player tracking pilot": "Pilote de suivi des joueurs", "The player-source pilot is unpublished. Workshop 0.3.0 tracks named entities; real-player lifecycle validation remains pending. See PLAYER-TRACKING-PILOT.md.": "Le pilote joueur n’est pas publié. Workshop 0.3.0 suit les entités nommées ; le cycle réel des joueurs reste à valider. Consultez PLAYER-TRACKING-PILOT.md.", "The unpublished player-source pilot uses the existing dedicated allowlist reader. Workshop 0.3.0 still supports named entities only. A server administrator selects current positive session playerIds and matching telemetry entityIds in private JSOC_ORBAT_Tracked.json, with source set to players. Maximum 60; use fresh pairing when changing selection or after a disconnect. Respawns retain the alias within the same connected controller. No automatic roster picker, platform identity transmission or 120-player support. Compilation and synthetic policy checks are separate from real-player validation. See PLAYER-TRACKING-PILOT.md before testing.": "Le pilote joueur non publié utilise le lecteur dédié existant. Workshop 0.3.0 suit uniquement les entités nommées. L’administrateur sélectionne les playerIds positifs de la session et les entityIds correspondants dans le fichier privé JSOC_ORBAT_Tracked.json, source players. Maximum 60 ; nouveau couplage après changement de sélection ou déconnexion. La réapparition conserve l’alias dans la même connexion. Aucun sélecteur automatique, identité de plateforme transmise ou support de 120 joueurs. Compilation et tests synthétiques ne remplacent pas un test avec de vrais joueurs. Consultez PLAYER-TRACKING-PILOT.md."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"Player tracking pilot": "Pilot für Spieler-Tracking", "The player-source pilot is unpublished. Workshop 0.3.0 tracks named entities; real-player lifecycle validation remains pending. See PLAYER-TRACKING-PILOT.md.": "Der Spieler-Pilot ist unveröffentlicht. Workshop 0.3.0 verfolgt benannte Entitäten; echte Spieler-Lebenszyklen sind noch zu prüfen. Siehe PLAYER-TRACKING-PILOT.md.", "The unpublished player-source pilot uses the existing dedicated allowlist reader. Workshop 0.3.0 still supports named entities only. A server administrator selects current positive session playerIds and matching telemetry entityIds in private JSOC_ORBAT_Tracked.json, with source set to players. Maximum 60; use fresh pairing when changing selection or after a disconnect. Respawns retain the alias within the same connected controller. No automatic roster picker, platform identity transmission or 120-player support. Compilation and synthetic policy checks are separate from real-player validation. See PLAYER-TRACKING-PILOT.md before testing.": "Der unveröffentlichte Spieler-Pilot nutzt den bestehenden dedizierten Leser. Workshop 0.3.0 verfolgt nur benannte Entitäten. Der Administrator wählt positive playerIds der aktuellen Sitzung und passende entityIds in der privaten JSOC_ORBAT_Tracked.json mit source players. Höchstens 60; nach Auswahländerung oder Trennung neu koppeln. Respawns behalten den Alias innerhalb derselben Verbindung. Keine automatische Spielerauswahl, Übertragung von Plattformidentitäten oder Unterstützung für 120 Spieler. Kompilierung und synthetische Tests ersetzen keinen echten Spielertest. Siehe PLAYER-TRACKING-PILOT.md."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"Host Local players / AI / factions — 60 slots (pilot)": "Host Local joueurs / IA / factions — 60 places (pilote)", "Allow reviewed GM requests — in-game host approval required (pilot)": "Autoriser les requêtes GM vérifiées — approbation de l’hôte dans le jeu (pilote)", "Review 1–16 selected units with verified prefab references. JSON exports remain intentions. Game requests execute only after in-game host approval.": "Vérifiez 1–16 unités avec des références prefab validées. Les exports JSON restent des intentions. Exécution uniquement après approbation dans le jeu.", "Send reviewed spawn request to game": "Envoyer la création vérifiée au jeu", "Check game request results": "Consulter les résultats du jeu", "Cancel pending game request": "Annuler la requête en attente", "Bridge-created group": "Groupe créé par le bridge", "Check game results first": "Consultez d’abord les résultats", "Choose a bridge-created group": "Choisir un groupe créé par le bridge", "Request removal of bridge-created group": "Demander le retrait du groupe créé par le bridge", "Spawn request pending in-game host approval": "Création en attente d’approbation dans le jeu", "Removal request pending in-game host approval": "Retrait en attente d’approbation dans le jeu", "Game request rejected": "Requête au jeu refusée", "No game requests": "Aucune requête au jeu", "No submitted game request": "Aucune requête envoyée", "Pending game request cancelled.": "Requête en attente annulée.", "Review selected units without changing the saved plan. The GM pilot can send spawn/remove requests with separate in-game host approval.": "Vérifiez les unités sans changer le plan enregistré. Le pilote GM peut envoyer des créations/retraits avec approbation séparée dans le jeu.", "In the GAME, open Host Pairing → Players / AI / factions. Enable factions and select units, then return to pairing. Paste this address and code and Connect. Uses host_1 through host_60 automatically. Requires the unpublished mixed-host candidate; Workshop 0.3.0 is insufficient.": "JEU : ouvrez Host Pairing → Players / AI / factions. Activez les factions et sélectionnez les unités, puis revenez au couplage. Collez cette adresse et ce code, puis Connect. Alias host_1 à host_60 automatiques. Le candidat mixte non publié est requis ; Workshop 0.3.0 ne suffit pas.", "Host Local: players, AI and factions": "Hôte local : joueurs, IA et factions", "In the GM pilot APP, Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles: choose Host Local players / AI / factions, then Connect profile. GAME: Host Pairing → Players / AI / factions. Enable the factions you want, choose humans and/or AI, Refresh roster, then select units or Select matching. The total cap is 60; aliases are assigned automatically. Return to pairing, paste the APP address into the first field and its code into the second, then Connect and resume. Slots remain reserved during a pairing. Use a fresh APP connection/code after disconnecting. Only standard GM-editable AI characters are discovered. The new native candidate is required; Workshop 0.3.0 does not contain these controls. Real Host Local lifecycle testing remains pending.": "APP pilote GM : Paramètres → Live bridge → Profils serveur. Choisissez joueurs / IA / factions Host Local, puis Connecter le profil. JEU : Host Pairing → Players / AI / factions. Activez les factions voulues et les joueurs humains et/ou l’IA, actualisez la liste puis sélectionnez les unités ou Select matching. Limite totale : 60 ; les alias sont automatiques. Revenez au couplage, collez l’adresse APP dans le premier champ et le code dans le second, puis Connect et reprenez. Les places restent réservées pendant le couplage. Après déconnexion, créez une nouvelle connexion/code APP. Seules les IA modifiables dans GM sont découvertes. Le nouveau candidat natif est requis ; Workshop 0.3.0 ne contient pas ces commandes. Le cycle Host Local réel reste à tester.", "GM pilot: approve spawn and removal": "Pilote GM : approuver création et retrait", "APP: enable Allow reviewed GM requests in a Host Local mixed profile before connecting. In Units → Deployment preview, review 1–16 units with verified prefab references and Send reviewed spawn request to game. GAME host: Review GM requests → Check pending, inspect every unit, then Approve or Reject. APP: Check game request results. Removal only targets a bridge-created group chosen from results and also requires game approval. Cancel pending game request works before approval. Pending requests expire after 60 seconds; approved execution has a 30-second window. Native terrain height and exact prefab identity are checked; rollback handles partial spawn failure. Up to 60 owned root objects and 100 commands per scene/pairing budget; prefab children can add more actors. Two synthetic native objects passed HTTPS spawn/remove, but the real Host Local panels and players/AI remain untested. AI orders, weather and live property edits are future work. See HOST-GM-PILOT.md.": "APP : activez les requêtes GM vérifiées dans un profil Host Local mixte avant connexion. Unités → Deployment preview : vérifiez 1–16 unités avec des prefabs identifiés, puis envoyez la requête au jeu. Hôte JEU : Review GM requests → Check pending, inspectez chaque unité puis Approve ou Reject. APP : consultez les résultats. Le retrait cible uniquement un groupe créé par le bridge choisi dans les résultats, avec approbation dans le jeu. Annulation possible avant approbation. Expiration : 60 secondes en attente, 30 secondes après approbation. Le moteur vérifie hauteur du terrain et identité du prefab ; une création partielle est annulée en cas d’échec. Limites : 60 objets racines possédés et 100 commandes selon le budget scène/couplage ; les enfants des prefabs peuvent ajouter des acteurs. Deux objets synthétiques ont passé le test natif HTTPS, mais les panneaux Host Local et joueurs/IA réels restent à tester. Ordres IA, météo et propriétés en direct restent à développer. Voir HOST-GM-PILOT.md."});
Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"Host Local players / AI / factions — 60 slots (pilot)": "Host Local Spieler / KI / Fraktionen — 60 Plätze (Pilot)", "Allow reviewed GM requests — in-game host approval required (pilot)": "Geprüfte GM-Anfragen erlauben — Bestätigung durch Spiel-Host erforderlich (Pilot)", "Review 1–16 selected units with verified prefab references. JSON exports remain intentions. Game requests execute only after in-game host approval.": "1–16 ausgewählte Einheiten mit geprüften Prefab-Referenzen prüfen. JSON-Exporte bleiben Absichten. Ausführung erst nach Bestätigung im Spiel.", "Send reviewed spawn request to game": "Geprüfte Spawn-Anfrage ans Spiel senden", "Check game request results": "Spielanfrage-Ergebnisse prüfen", "Cancel pending game request": "Wartende Spielanfrage abbrechen", "Bridge-created group": "Vom Bridge erzeugte Gruppe", "Check game results first": "Zuerst Spielergebnisse prüfen", "Choose a bridge-created group": "Vom Bridge erzeugte Gruppe wählen", "Request removal of bridge-created group": "Entfernung einer Bridge-Gruppe anfordern", "Spawn request pending in-game host approval": "Spawn-Anfrage wartet auf Spielbestätigung", "Removal request pending in-game host approval": "Entfernung wartet auf Spielbestätigung", "Game request rejected": "Spielanfrage abgelehnt", "No game requests": "Keine Spielanfragen", "No submitted game request": "Keine gesendete Spielanfrage", "Pending game request cancelled.": "Wartende Spielanfrage abgebrochen.", "Review selected units without changing the saved plan. The GM pilot can send spawn/remove requests with separate in-game host approval.": "Einheiten prüfen, ohne den gespeicherten Plan zu ändern. GM-Pilot kann Spawn/Entfernung mit separater Spielbestätigung anfordern.", "In the GAME, open Host Pairing → Players / AI / factions. Enable factions and select units, then return to pairing. Paste this address and code and Connect. Uses host_1 through host_60 automatically. Requires the unpublished mixed-host candidate; Workshop 0.3.0 is insufficient.": "SPIEL: Host Pairing → Players / AI / factions öffnen. Fraktionen aktivieren und Einheiten wählen, dann zur Kopplung zurückkehren. Diese Adresse und Code einfügen und Connect. host_1 bis host_60 automatisch. Neuer unveröffentlichter Kandidat erforderlich; Workshop 0.3.0 reicht nicht.", "Host Local: players, AI and factions": "Lokaler Host: Spieler, KI und Fraktionen", "In the GM pilot APP, Settings → Live bridge → Server profiles: choose Host Local players / AI / factions, then Connect profile. GAME: Host Pairing → Players / AI / factions. Enable the factions you want, choose humans and/or AI, Refresh roster, then select units or Select matching. The total cap is 60; aliases are assigned automatically. Return to pairing, paste the APP address into the first field and its code into the second, then Connect and resume. Slots remain reserved during a pairing. Use a fresh APP connection/code after disconnecting. Only standard GM-editable AI characters are discovered. The new native candidate is required; Workshop 0.3.0 does not contain these controls. Real Host Local lifecycle testing remains pending.": "GM-Pilot-APP: Einstellungen → Live bridge → Serverprofile. Host Local players / AI / factions wählen und Profil verbinden. SPIEL: Host Pairing → Players / AI / factions. Gewünschte Fraktionen und Menschen/KI aktivieren, Liste aktualisieren, Einheiten oder Select matching wählen. Insgesamt höchstens 60; Aliase werden automatisch vergeben. Zur Kopplung zurückkehren, APP-Adresse ins erste Feld und Code ins zweite einfügen, Connect und Spiel fortsetzen. Plätze bleiben während der Kopplung reserviert. Nach Trennung neue APP-Verbindung/Code erstellen. Nur im GM bearbeitbare KI-Charaktere werden erfasst. Neuer nativer Kandidat erforderlich; Workshop 0.3.0 enthält diese Steuerung nicht. Echte Host-Local-Lebenszyklen müssen noch geprüft werden.", "GM pilot: approve spawn and removal": "GM-Pilot: Spawn und Entfernung bestätigen", "APP: enable Allow reviewed GM requests in a Host Local mixed profile before connecting. In Units → Deployment preview, review 1–16 units with verified prefab references and Send reviewed spawn request to game. GAME host: Review GM requests → Check pending, inspect every unit, then Approve or Reject. APP: Check game request results. Removal only targets a bridge-created group chosen from results and also requires game approval. Cancel pending game request works before approval. Pending requests expire after 60 seconds; approved execution has a 30-second window. Native terrain height and exact prefab identity are checked; rollback handles partial spawn failure. Up to 60 owned root objects and 100 commands per scene/pairing budget; prefab children can add more actors. Two synthetic native objects passed HTTPS spawn/remove, but the real Host Local panels and players/AI remain untested. AI orders, weather and live property edits are future work. See HOST-GM-PILOT.md.": "APP: Vor dem Verbinden geprüfte GM-Anfragen im gemischten Host-Local-Profil aktivieren. Einheiten → Deployment preview: 1–16 Einheiten mit geprüften Prefab-Referenzen prüfen und Spawn-Anfrage senden. SPIEL-Host: Review GM requests → Check pending, jede Einheit ansehen, dann Approve oder Reject. APP: Ergebnisse prüfen. Entfernung betrifft nur eine aus den Ergebnissen gewählte, vom Bridge erzeugte Gruppe und braucht ebenfalls Spielbestätigung. Abbruch ist vor Bestätigung möglich. Ablauf: 60 Sekunden wartend, 30 Sekunden nach Bestätigung. Engine prüft Geländehöhe und genaue Prefab-Identität; Teil-Spawns werden bei Fehler zurückgerollt. Höchstens 60 eigene Wurzelobjekte und 100 Befehle im Szenen/Kopplungsbudget; Prefab-Kinder können weitere Akteure erzeugen. Zwei synthetische Objekte bestanden den nativen HTTPS-Test; echte Host-Local-Panels und Spieler/KI sind noch zu prüfen. KI-Befehle, Wetter und Live-Eigenschaftsänderungen folgen später. Siehe HOST-GM-PILOT.md."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"In Units, select 1–16 units with reviewed prefab assets. Open Deployment preview, load the matching resource index, set heading and Review selected units. Check GUID provenance, positions and required addons. Export reviewed deployment JSON remains intention-only. The GM pilot additionally sends spawn requests for separate in-game host approval; see the GM pilot topic. Plan, heading or source changes require a new review. Missing addon metadata is shown; native resources and terrain are checked by the game. Settings → Deployment preview opens this panel.": "Unités : sélectionnez 1–16 unités avec des prefabs vérifiés. Ouvrez Deployment preview, chargez l’index correspondant, réglez l’orientation et vérifiez les unités. Contrôlez provenance GUID, positions et addons. L’export JSON reste une intention. Le pilote GM permet aussi les requêtes de création avec approbation séparée dans le jeu ; voir sa rubrique. Tout changement de plan, orientation ou source impose une nouvelle vérification. Les métadonnées manquantes sont signalées ; le jeu vérifie ressources et terrain. Paramètres → Deployment preview ouvre le panneau."});
Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"In Units, select 1–16 units with reviewed prefab assets. Open Deployment preview, load the matching resource index, set heading and Review selected units. Check GUID provenance, positions and required addons. Export reviewed deployment JSON remains intention-only. The GM pilot additionally sends spawn requests for separate in-game host approval; see the GM pilot topic. Plan, heading or source changes require a new review. Missing addon metadata is shown; native resources and terrain are checked by the game. Settings → Deployment preview opens this panel.": "In Einheiten 1–16 Einheiten mit geprüften Prefabs wählen. Deployment preview öffnen, passenden Index laden, Richtung festlegen und prüfen. GUID-Herkunft, Positionen und Addons kontrollieren. JSON-Export bleibt Absicht. GM-Pilot erlaubt zusätzlich Spawn-Anfragen mit separater Spielbestätigung; siehe GM-Thema. Plan-, Richtungs- oder Quellenänderungen erfordern neue Prüfung. Fehlende Metadaten werden angezeigt; Spiel prüft Ressourcen und Terrain. Einstellungen → Deployment preview öffnet das Panel."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"GM pilot: Host Local players and standard GM-editable AI share 60 slots with faction filters. Reviewed spawn/remove requests require explicit opt-in and in-game approval. Requires the new native candidate; see HOST-GM-PILOT.md.": "Pilote GM : joueurs Host Local et IA modifiables dans GM partagent 60 places et des filtres de faction. Création/retrait vérifiés : autorisation explicite et approbation dans le jeu. Nouveau candidat natif requis ; voir HOST-GM-PILOT.md."});
Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"GM pilot: Host Local players and standard GM-editable AI share 60 slots with faction filters. Reviewed spawn/remove requests require explicit opt-in and in-game approval. Requires the new native candidate; see HOST-GM-PILOT.md.": "GM-Pilot: Host-Local-Spieler und im GM bearbeitbare KI teilen 60 Plätze mit Fraktionsfiltern. Geprüfter Spawn/Entfernung braucht ausdrückliche Freigabe und Spielbestätigung. Neuer nativer Kandidat erforderlich; siehe HOST-GM-PILOT.md."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"Map image alignment is reversed for native world X/Z. Saved planner positions remain unchanged.": "L’alignement de l’image est inversé pour les coordonnées natives X/Z. Les positions du plan enregistré restent inchangées."});
Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"Map image alignment is reversed for native world X/Z. Saved planner positions remain unchanged.": "Die Bildausrichtung wird für native Weltkoordinaten X/Z zurückgerechnet. Gespeicherte Planpositionen bleiben unverändert."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"APP: enable Allow reviewed GM requests in a Host Local mixed profile before connecting. In Units → Deployment preview, review 1–16 units with verified prefab references and Send reviewed spawn request to game. GAME host: Review GM requests → Check pending, inspect every unit, then Approve or Reject. APP: Check game request results. Removal only targets a bridge-created group chosen from results and also requires game approval. Cancel pending game request works before approval. Pending requests expire after 60 seconds; approved execution has a 30-second window. Native terrain height and exact prefab identity are checked; rollback handles partial spawn failure. Up to 60 owned root objects and 100 commands per scene/pairing budget; prefab children can add more actors. Two synthetic native objects passed HTTPS spawn/remove, but the real Host Local panels and players/AI remain untested. AI orders, weather and live property edits are future work. See HOST-GM-PILOT.md. Native spawn/export coordinates reverse the map imagery offset: world X/Z are 50 m lower than the saved map coordinates. The planned marker stays in place.":"APP : activez les requêtes GM vérifiées dans un profil Host Local mixte avant connexion. Unités → Deployment preview : vérifiez 1–16 unités avec des prefabs identifiés, puis envoyez la requête au jeu. Hôte JEU : Review GM requests → Check pending, inspectez chaque unité puis Approve ou Reject. APP : consultez les résultats. Le retrait cible uniquement un groupe créé par le bridge choisi dans les résultats, avec approbation dans le jeu. Annulation possible avant approbation. Expiration : 60 secondes en attente, 30 secondes après approbation. Le moteur vérifie hauteur du terrain et identité du prefab ; une création partielle est annulée en cas d’échec. Limites : 60 objets racines possédés et 100 commandes selon le budget scène/couplage ; les enfants des prefabs peuvent ajouter des acteurs. Deux objets synthétiques ont passé le test natif HTTPS, mais les panneaux Host Local et joueurs/IA réels restent à tester. Ordres IA, météo et propriétés en direct restent à développer. Voir HOST-GM-PILOT.md. La conversion native retire 50 m des coordonnées cartographiques X/Z. Le marqueur et les positions enregistrées ne bougent pas."});
Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"APP: enable Allow reviewed GM requests in a Host Local mixed profile before connecting. In Units → Deployment preview, review 1–16 units with verified prefab references and Send reviewed spawn request to game. GAME host: Review GM requests → Check pending, inspect every unit, then Approve or Reject. APP: Check game request results. Removal only targets a bridge-created group chosen from results and also requires game approval. Cancel pending game request works before approval. Pending requests expire after 60 seconds; approved execution has a 30-second window. Native terrain height and exact prefab identity are checked; rollback handles partial spawn failure. Up to 60 owned root objects and 100 commands per scene/pairing budget; prefab children can add more actors. Two synthetic native objects passed HTTPS spawn/remove, but the real Host Local panels and players/AI remain untested. AI orders, weather and live property edits are future work. See HOST-GM-PILOT.md. Native spawn/export coordinates reverse the map imagery offset: world X/Z are 50 m lower than the saved map coordinates. The planned marker stays in place.":"APP: Vor dem Verbinden geprüfte GM-Anfragen im gemischten Host-Local-Profil aktivieren. Einheiten → Deployment preview: 1–16 Einheiten mit geprüften Prefab-Referenzen prüfen und Spawn-Anfrage senden. SPIEL-Host: Review GM requests → Check pending, jede Einheit ansehen, dann Approve oder Reject. APP: Ergebnisse prüfen. Entfernung betrifft nur eine aus den Ergebnissen gewählte, vom Bridge erzeugte Gruppe und braucht ebenfalls Spielbestätigung. Abbruch ist vor Bestätigung möglich. Ablauf: 60 Sekunden wartend, 30 Sekunden nach Bestätigung. Engine prüft Geländehöhe und genaue Prefab-Identität; Teil-Spawns werden bei Fehler zurückgerollt. Höchstens 60 eigene Wurzelobjekte und 100 Befehle im Szenen/Kopplungsbudget; Prefab-Kinder können weitere Akteure erzeugen. Zwei synthetische Objekte bestanden den nativen HTTPS-Test; echte Host-Local-Panels und Spieler/KI sind noch zu prüfen. KI-Befehle, Wetter und Live-Eigenschaftsänderungen folgen später. Siehe HOST-GM-PILOT.md. Die native Umrechnung zieht 50 m von Karten-X/Z ab. Marker und gespeicherte Positionen bleiben unverändert."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"In Assets, use Import catalog JSON. The COMMAND Vanilla-Assets bundle provides ready-to-import files: start with Start-Here/01-Operational-Assets-Catalog.json (2,721 entries). For GM deployment review, load its matching 01-Operational-Assets-Resource-Index.json. Complete-Catalog contains all 19,438 indexed base-game prefab identities by category. Import one compatible part at a time; importing another catalog replaces the chooser list, while assigned units retain their snapshots. Choose Assigned asset from your JSON in Units and set faction separately. Metadata GUIDs do not prove that every base template, damaged variant or helper can spawn alone. Modded assets use the existing reviewed metadata workflow. Export planning catalog includes session entries and assigned snapshots; reimport after restart. Catalog import/export does not edit the mission, and conflicting snapshots block export.":"Dans Assets, utilisez Import catalog JSON. Le pack COMMAND Vanilla-Assets contient des fichiers prêts à importer : commencez par Start-Here/01-Operational-Assets-Catalog.json (2 721 entrées). Pour vérifier un déploiement GM, chargez le fichier 01-Operational-Assets-Resource-Index.json correspondant. Complete-Catalog contient les 19 438 identités de prefabs du jeu de base, classées par catégorie. Importez une partie compatible à la fois : un nouveau catalogue remplace la liste active, mais les unités conservent leurs références. Choisissez Assigned asset from your JSON dans Units et définissez la faction séparément. Une GUID ne garantit pas que les modèles de base, variantes endommagées ou éléments auxiliaires puissent être créés seuls. Les mods utilisent le processus existant de métadonnées vérifiées. Export planning catalog inclut les entrées actives et les références assignées ; réimportez après un redémarrage. Les catalogues ne modifient pas la mission. Des références contradictoires bloquent l’export."});
Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"In Assets, use Import catalog JSON. The COMMAND Vanilla-Assets bundle provides ready-to-import files: start with Start-Here/01-Operational-Assets-Catalog.json (2,721 entries). For GM deployment review, load its matching 01-Operational-Assets-Resource-Index.json. Complete-Catalog contains all 19,438 indexed base-game prefab identities by category. Import one compatible part at a time; importing another catalog replaces the chooser list, while assigned units retain their snapshots. Choose Assigned asset from your JSON in Units and set faction separately. Metadata GUIDs do not prove that every base template, damaged variant or helper can spawn alone. Modded assets use the existing reviewed metadata workflow. Export planning catalog includes session entries and assigned snapshots; reimport after restart. Catalog import/export does not edit the mission, and conflicting snapshots block export.":"Verwenden Sie unter Assets die Funktion Import catalog JSON. Das Paket COMMAND Vanilla-Assets enthält fertige Dateien: Beginnen Sie mit Start-Here/01-Operational-Assets-Catalog.json (2.721 Einträge). Laden Sie zur GM-Deployment-Prüfung die passende Datei 01-Operational-Assets-Resource-Index.json. Complete-Catalog enthält alle 19.438 erfassten Basis-Spiel-Prefab-Identitäten nach Kategorie. Importieren Sie jeweils einen passenden Teil: Ein neuer Katalog ersetzt die aktive Liste; zugewiesene Einheiten behalten ihre Referenzen. Wählen Sie unter Units Assigned asset from your JSON und legen Sie die Fraktion separat fest. Eine GUID bestätigt nicht, dass jedes Basistemplate, jede beschädigte Variante oder jeder Helfer einzeln erzeugt werden kann. Mods nutzen den bestehenden Metadaten-Prüfprozess. Export planning catalog enthält aktive Einträge und zugewiesene Referenzen; importieren Sie den Katalog nach dem Neustart erneut. Kataloge verändern die Mission nicht. Widersprüchliche Referenzen blockieren den Export."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"All asset types": "Tous les types", "Troops": "Soldats", "Vehicles": "Véhicules", "Groups": "Groupes", "Weapons": "Armes", "Equipment": "Équipement", "Structures": "Structures", "Props": "Objets", "Other / unclassified": "Autres / non classés", "Search assets": "Rechercher des ressources", "Search name, faction, path or GUID": "Nom, faction, chemin ou GUID", "Asset type": "Type de ressource", "Asset faction": "Faction de la ressource", "All asset factions": "Toutes les factions", "Unspecified": "Non précisé", "Include base templates and damaged variants": "Inclure les modèles de base et variantes endommagées", "Previous": "Précédent", "Next": "Suivant", "Clear asset assignment": "Retirer la ressource attribuée", "Browse assets": "Parcourir les ressources", "matching assets": "ressources correspondantes", "Template / variant": "Modèle / variante", "No assets match these filters.": "Aucune ressource ne correspond à ces filtres.", "Types and factions are catalog hints. Native spawn availability still requires validation. Choose an asset, then Apply changes or Place new unit.": "Les types et factions sont des indications du catalogue. La création native reste à vérifier. Choisissez une ressource, puis appliquez les changements ou placez une unité.", "Selected unit needs a name. Enter a name in Units, click Apply changes, then review again.": "L’unité sélectionnée a besoin d’un nom. Saisissez-le dans Unités, appliquez les changements, puis relancez la vérification.", "Selected unit name must be 1–160 characters without control characters. Update it in Units and Apply changes.": "Le nom doit contenir 1 à 160 caractères sans caractères de contrôle. Corrigez-le dans Unités et appliquez les changements."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"All asset types": "Alle Ressourcentypen", "Troops": "Soldaten", "Vehicles": "Fahrzeuge", "Groups": "Gruppen", "Weapons": "Waffen", "Equipment": "Ausrüstung", "Structures": "Bauwerke", "Props": "Objekte", "Other / unclassified": "Andere / unklassifiziert", "Search assets": "Ressourcen suchen", "Search name, faction, path or GUID": "Name, Fraktion, Pfad oder GUID", "Asset type": "Ressourcentyp", "Asset faction": "Ressourcenfraktion", "All asset factions": "Alle Ressourcenfraktionen", "Unspecified": "Nicht angegeben", "Include base templates and damaged variants": "Basistemplates und beschädigte Varianten anzeigen", "Previous": "Zurück", "Next": "Weiter", "Clear asset assignment": "Ressourcenzuweisung entfernen", "Browse assets": "Ressourcen durchsuchen", "matching assets": "passende Ressourcen", "Template / variant": "Template / Variante", "No assets match these filters.": "Keine Ressourcen entsprechen diesen Filtern.", "Types and factions are catalog hints. Native spawn availability still requires validation. Choose an asset, then Apply changes or Place new unit.": "Typen und Fraktionen sind Kataloghinweise. Native Erzeugung muss weiterhin geprüft werden. Ressource wählen, dann Änderungen anwenden oder neue Einheit platzieren.", "Selected unit needs a name. Enter a name in Units, click Apply changes, then review again.": "Die ausgewählte Einheit benötigt einen Namen. Unter Einheiten eingeben, Änderungen anwenden und erneut prüfen.", "Selected unit name must be 1–160 characters without control characters. Update it in Units and Apply changes.": "Der Einheitenname muss 1–160 Zeichen ohne Steuerzeichen enthalten. Unter Einheiten korrigieren und Änderungen anwenden."});

window.PlannerTranslations.fr["In Assets, use Import catalog JSON. The COMMAND Vanilla-Assets bundle provides ready-to-import files: start with Start-Here/01-Operational-Assets-Catalog.json (2,721 entries). For GM deployment review, load its matching 01-Operational-Assets-Resource-Index.json. Complete-Catalog contains all 19,438 indexed base-game prefab identities by category. Import one compatible part at a time; importing another catalog replaces the chooser list, while assigned units retain their snapshots. Choose Assigned asset from your JSON in Units and set faction separately. Metadata GUIDs do not prove that every base template, damaged variant or helper can spawn alone. Modded assets use the existing reviewed metadata workflow. Export planning catalog includes session entries and assigned snapshots; reimport after restart. Catalog import/export does not edit the mission, and conflicting snapshots block export. In Units, Browse assets opens a searchable list with asset type and prefab faction filters. Search by readable name, path or GUID; use Previous and Next for more results. Base templates and damaged variants can be hidden. Select an asset, then Apply changes for an existing unit or Place new unit. Browsing and filtering do not edit the mission or change the unit faction."]=window.PlannerTranslations.fr["In Assets, use Import catalog JSON. The COMMAND Vanilla-Assets bundle provides ready-to-import files: start with Start-Here/01-Operational-Assets-Catalog.json (2,721 entries). For GM deployment review, load its matching 01-Operational-Assets-Resource-Index.json. Complete-Catalog contains all 19,438 indexed base-game prefab identities by category. Import one compatible part at a time; importing another catalog replaces the chooser list, while assigned units retain their snapshots. Choose Assigned asset from your JSON in Units and set faction separately. Metadata GUIDs do not prove that every base template, damaged variant or helper can spawn alone. Modded assets use the existing reviewed metadata workflow. Export planning catalog includes session entries and assigned snapshots; reimport after restart. Catalog import/export does not edit the mission, and conflicting snapshots block export."]+" Dans Unités, Parcourir les ressources ouvre une liste avec recherche et filtres par type et faction du prefab. Recherchez un nom, chemin ou GUID ; utilisez Précédent et Suivant. Les modèles de base et variantes endommagées peuvent être masqués. Choisissez une ressource, puis appliquez les changements ou placez une unité. Les filtres ne modifient ni la mission ni la faction de l’unité.";

