Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"SQF syntax inspector": "Inspecteur de syntaxe SQF", "Inspect nested conditions, loops and stored code blocks. Expressions and runtime semantics remain unresolved. This does not generate Enforce code or run game commands.": "Examinez conditions imbriquées, boucles et blocs de code stockés. Expressions et sémantique restent non résolues. Aucun code Enforce ni ordre de jeu n’est exécuté.", "Inspect SQF structure": "Examiner la structure SQF", "No syntax review": "Aucun examen syntaxique", "Previous syntax rows": "Lignes syntaxiques précédentes", "Next syntax rows": "Lignes syntaxiques suivantes", "Export syntax review": "Exporter l’examen syntaxique", "Clear syntax review": "Effacer l’examen syntaxique", "Syntax review is stale. Inspect again.": "Examen syntaxique périmé. Examinez à nouveau.", "Inspecting SQF structure": "Examen de la structure SQF", "Syntax review timed out": "Délai de l’examen syntaxique dépassé", "Syntax review ready": "Examen syntaxique prêt", "Syntax review rejected": "Examen syntaxique rejeté", "Syntax review saved": "Examen syntaxique enregistré", "Syntax export cancelled": "Export syntaxique annulé", "Syntax export failed": "Échec de l’export syntaxique", "Open SQF syntax inspector": "Ouvrir l’inspecteur de syntaxe SQF", "Source file": "Fichier source", "Code block": "Bloc de code", "Condition": "Condition", "Exit current code scope": "Quitter la portée actuelle", "While loop": "Boucle while", "Range loop": "Boucle à intervalle", "Three-block loop": "Boucle à trois blocs", "For-each loop": "Boucle forEach", "Stored code block": "Bloc de code stocké", "Assignment": "Affectation", "Code value": "Valeur de code", "Unresolved expression or command": "Expression ou commande non résolue", "Unsupported control syntax": "Syntaxe de contrôle non prise en charge", "Review finding": "Point à examiner", "syntax nodes": "nœuds syntaxiques", "loops": "boucles", "conditions": "conditions", "unsupported statements": "instructions non prises en charge"});

window.PlannerTranslations.de["In Assets, use Import catalog JSON. The COMMAND Vanilla-Assets bundle provides ready-to-import files: start with Start-Here/01-Operational-Assets-Catalog.json (2,721 entries). For GM deployment review, load its matching 01-Operational-Assets-Resource-Index.json. Complete-Catalog contains all 19,438 indexed base-game prefab identities by category. Import one compatible part at a time; importing another catalog replaces the chooser list, while assigned units retain their snapshots. Choose Assigned asset from your JSON in Units and set faction separately. Metadata GUIDs do not prove that every base template, damaged variant or helper can spawn alone. Modded assets use the existing reviewed metadata workflow. Export planning catalog includes session entries and assigned snapshots; reimport after restart. Catalog import/export does not edit the mission, and conflicting snapshots block export. In Units, Browse assets opens a searchable list with asset type and prefab faction filters. Search by readable name, path or GUID; use Previous and Next for more results. Base templates and damaged variants can be hidden. Select an asset, then Apply changes for an existing unit or Place new unit. Browsing and filtering do not edit the mission or change the unit faction. Military unit type also sets a matching asset filter: Infantry shows troops and Armor shows armoured vehicles. Choose All asset types to override it. Assets → Arma 3 migration review accepts dropped SQF, SQM, EXT and HPP files. It inventories commands, literal coordinates, classes and dependencies and exports a read-only conversion review. It never executes SQF or changes your mission. Movement bindings are advisory; asset mapping, terrain alignment, control flow and native validation remain required. Arma 3 asset mappings loads a target resource index and provides searchable prefab cards with type filters. Select a detected source class and exact target, inspect addon/GUID/path, then Confirm class mapping. Export a portable mapping file and reload it for reuse. Compatible index changes retain mappings; incompatible ones are rejected. Mapping is declared identity review, not proof of gameplay equivalence or native spawn availability. Prepare migration mission draft runs a bounded supported-pattern parser in a worker. Literal declarations, mapped unit/vehicle spawns, doMove and basic addWaypoint produce source-linked non-executable drafts. Conditions, loops, dynamic calls and unsupported statements remain unresolved. Source or mapping changes make the draft stale and disable export. Prepare again, inspect the blockers, then Export mission draft. No plan edits, native spawning or source script execution occur. Place migration units on the planner adds selected mapped spawn intents only. Name the source terrain, enter a matching source ground anchor and Everon world X/Z anchor, and optional counterclockwise rotation; distances stay in metres. Choose each unit’s planning faction/type, acknowledge unresolved height/groups/behaviour, then Preview planning placement and Add reviewed units to plan. Source, mappings, anchors or mission edits stale the preview. One Undo/Redo restores the entire planning batch. Optional reviewed linked movements can become proposed planning routes; scripts stay in review and no game command runs. Under Linked movement routes, select points associated with your selected source-created units and acknowledge that source timing is not reproduced. Up to 240 points form at most one proposed route per selected unit, in source order. One Undo/Redo covers units and routes together. Unselecting a unit clears its movement selection. Group addWaypoint and unresolved targets remain in review. Route/source links are provenance snapshots, not automatic binding after you edit or delete planner objects. Check terrain landmarks accepts 3–12 matching source east/north and Everon world X/Z pairs. Check landmark alignment fits translation/rotation without scaling, then shows per-point, maximum and RMS mismatch. Review coverage and residuals, tick its review box, then Use checked landmark alignment. A mismatch beyond your chosen 0.1–100 metre tolerance blocks placement; editing points or tolerance invalidates the fit. Narrow coverage is flagged. Manual single-anchor placement remains available when checked alignment is off. Saved planning provenance includes the fitted landmarks and diagnostics, while terrain identity and height stay unverified. Terrain identity and ground height is optional. Enter the exact target-world addon ID and qualified {GUID}world.ent resource, choose server-ground or imported-sample planning preview, and review compatibility with the Everon map. Source altitude is retained but not copied to target height. A ground report must match the world and each selected unit/route position within one centimetre; missing samples block sampled imports. Imported files are not live attestations. These explicitly terrain-reviewed units remain planning-only because the current bridge cannot enforce their world identity; deployment review rejects them instead of dropping that requirement. The separate opt-in diagnostic sampler reads the loaded world identity and GetSurfaceY into a profile report without spawning or modifying entities. Export terrain sampler query saves the current preview positions for the separate diagnostic addon. Put the query in that isolated server profile, run it on the intended loaded world, then load COMMAND-terrain-observation.json back into Companion and review again. Never treat a file as authenticated live state; use a fresh output/profile to avoid confusing an old report. SQF syntax inspector is a separate read-only view under Arma 3 migration review. Select source files, open SQF syntax inspector and choose Inspect SQF structure. It shows supported nested conditions, loop forms, stored code blocks and source locations in pages of 40 rows. Expressions, variable scope, scheduling and native semantics remain unresolved; unsupported syntax is retained with review findings. Export syntax review saves a non-executable structural AST JSON, not Enforce code or game commands. Source changes make the review stale and disable export until you inspect again. Clearing the review does not edit the mission. Settings also provides Open SQF syntax inspector."]=window.PlannerTranslations.de["In Assets, use Import catalog JSON. The COMMAND Vanilla-Assets bundle provides ready-to-import files: start with Start-Here/01-Operational-Assets-Catalog.json (2,721 entries). For GM deployment review, load its matching 01-Operational-Assets-Resource-Index.json. Complete-Catalog contains all 19,438 indexed base-game prefab identities by category. Import one compatible part at a time; importing another catalog replaces the chooser list, while assigned units retain their snapshots. Choose Assigned asset from your JSON in Units and set faction separately. Metadata GUIDs do not prove that every base template, damaged variant or helper can spawn alone. Modded assets use the existing reviewed metadata workflow. Export planning catalog includes session entries and assigned snapshots; reimport after restart. Catalog import/export does not edit the mission, and conflicting snapshots block export. In Units, Browse assets opens a searchable list with asset type and prefab faction filters. Search by readable name, path or GUID; use Previous and Next for more results. Base templates and damaged variants can be hidden. Select an asset, then Apply changes for an existing unit or Place new unit. Browsing and filtering do not edit the mission or change the unit faction. Military unit type also sets a matching asset filter: Infantry shows troops and Armor shows armoured vehicles. Choose All asset types to override it. Assets → Arma 3 migration review accepts dropped SQF, SQM, EXT and HPP files. It inventories commands, literal coordinates, classes and dependencies and exports a read-only conversion review. It never executes SQF or changes your mission. Movement bindings are advisory; asset mapping, terrain alignment, control flow and native validation remain required. Arma 3 asset mappings loads a target resource index and provides searchable prefab cards with type filters. Select a detected source class and exact target, inspect addon/GUID/path, then Confirm class mapping. Export a portable mapping file and reload it for reuse. Compatible index changes retain mappings; incompatible ones are rejected. Mapping is declared identity review, not proof of gameplay equivalence or native spawn availability. Prepare migration mission draft runs a bounded supported-pattern parser in a worker. Literal declarations, mapped unit/vehicle spawns, doMove and basic addWaypoint produce source-linked non-executable drafts. Conditions, loops, dynamic calls and unsupported statements remain unresolved. Source or mapping changes make the draft stale and disable export. Prepare again, inspect the blockers, then Export mission draft. No plan edits, native spawning or source script execution occur. Place migration units on the planner adds selected mapped spawn intents only. Name the source terrain, enter a matching source ground anchor and Everon world X/Z anchor, and optional counterclockwise rotation; distances stay in metres. Choose each unit’s planning faction/type, acknowledge unresolved height/groups/behaviour, then Preview planning placement and Add reviewed units to plan. Source, mappings, anchors or mission edits stale the preview. One Undo/Redo restores the entire planning batch. Optional reviewed linked movements can become proposed planning routes; scripts stay in review and no game command runs. Under Linked movement routes, select points associated with your selected source-created units and acknowledge that source timing is not reproduced. Up to 240 points form at most one proposed route per selected unit, in source order. One Undo/Redo covers units and routes together. Unselecting a unit clears its movement selection. Group addWaypoint and unresolved targets remain in review. Route/source links are provenance snapshots, not automatic binding after you edit or delete planner objects. Check terrain landmarks accepts 3–12 matching source east/north and Everon world X/Z pairs. Check landmark alignment fits translation/rotation without scaling, then shows per-point, maximum and RMS mismatch. Review coverage and residuals, tick its review box, then Use checked landmark alignment. A mismatch beyond your chosen 0.1–100 metre tolerance blocks placement; editing points or tolerance invalidates the fit. Narrow coverage is flagged. Manual single-anchor placement remains available when checked alignment is off. Saved planning provenance includes the fitted landmarks and diagnostics, while terrain identity and height stay unverified. Terrain identity and ground height is optional. Enter the exact target-world addon ID and qualified {GUID}world.ent resource, choose server-ground or imported-sample planning preview, and review compatibility with the Everon map. Source altitude is retained but not copied to target height. A ground report must match the world and each selected unit/route position within one centimetre; missing samples block sampled imports. Imported files are not live attestations. These explicitly terrain-reviewed units remain planning-only because the current bridge cannot enforce their world identity; deployment review rejects them instead of dropping that requirement. The separate opt-in diagnostic sampler reads the loaded world identity and GetSurfaceY into a profile report without spawning or modifying entities. Export terrain sampler query saves the current preview positions for the separate diagnostic addon. Put the query in that isolated server profile, run it on the intended loaded world, then load COMMAND-terrain-observation.json back into Companion and review again. Never treat a file as authenticated live state; use a fresh output/profile to avoid confusing an old report."]+" Der SQF-Syntaxinspektor ist eine separate schreibgeschützte Ansicht in der Arma-3-Migrationsprüfung. Dateien auswählen und SQF-Struktur prüfen: verschachtelte Bedingungen, Schleifen und gespeicherte Blöcke mit Quellpositionen, in Seiten zu 40 Zeilen. Ausdrücke, Gültigkeitsbereiche, Ablaufplanung und native Semantik bleiben ungeklärt. Nicht unterstützte Syntax bleibt mit Prüfhinweisen erhalten. Syntaxprüfung exportieren speichert nicht ausführbares AST-JSON, keinen Enforce-Code oder Spielbefehl. Quelländerungen machen die Prüfung ungültig und sperren den Export bis zur erneuten Prüfung. Löschen verändert die Mission nicht. Auch die Einstellungen öffnen diesen Inspektor.";
Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"SQF syntax inspector": "SQF-Syntaxinspektor", "Inspect nested conditions, loops and stored code blocks. Expressions and runtime semantics remain unresolved. This does not generate Enforce code or run game commands.": "Verschachtelte Bedingungen, Schleifen und gespeicherte Codeblöcke prüfen. Ausdrücke und Laufzeitsemantik bleiben ungeklärt. Es wird kein Enforce-Code erzeugt und kein Spielbefehl ausgeführt.", "Inspect SQF structure": "SQF-Struktur prüfen", "No syntax review": "Keine Syntaxprüfung", "Previous syntax rows": "Vorherige Syntaxzeilen", "Next syntax rows": "Nächste Syntaxzeilen", "Export syntax review": "Syntaxprüfung exportieren", "Clear syntax review": "Syntaxprüfung löschen", "Syntax review is stale. Inspect again.": "Syntaxprüfung veraltet. Erneut prüfen.", "Inspecting SQF structure": "SQF-Struktur wird geprüft", "Syntax review timed out": "Zeitlimit der Syntaxprüfung überschritten", "Syntax review ready": "Syntaxprüfung bereit", "Syntax review rejected": "Syntaxprüfung abgelehnt", "Syntax review saved": "Syntaxprüfung gespeichert", "Syntax export cancelled": "Syntaxexport abgebrochen", "Syntax export failed": "Syntaxexport fehlgeschlagen", "Open SQF syntax inspector": "SQF-Syntaxinspektor öffnen", "Source file": "Quelldatei", "Code block": "Codeblock", "Condition": "Bedingung", "Exit current code scope": "Aktuellen Codebereich verlassen", "While loop": "While-Schleife", "Range loop": "Bereichsschleife", "Three-block loop": "Dreiblock-Schleife", "For-each loop": "ForEach-Schleife", "Stored code block": "Gespeicherter Codeblock", "Assignment": "Zuweisung", "Code value": "Codewert", "Unresolved expression or command": "Ungeklärter Ausdruck oder Befehl", "Unsupported control syntax": "Nicht unterstützte Kontrollsyntax", "Review finding": "Prüfhinweis", "syntax nodes": "Syntaxknoten", "loops": "Schleifen", "conditions": "Bedingungen", "unsupported statements": "nicht unterstützte Anweisungen"});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.fr,{"Source dependency inspector": "Inspecteur des dépendances source", "Select loose source files or one source-package JSON. Only selected sources are inspected; includes are not loaded or executed.": "Sélectionnez les sources ou un paquet JSON. Seuls les fichiers choisis sont inspectés ; les inclusions ne sont ni chargées ni exécutées.", "Choose and inspect source files": "Choisir et inspecter les sources", "Cancel dependency inspection": "Annuler l’inspection", "Search dependency findings": "Rechercher dans les dépendances", "Dependency rows": "Résultats de dépendances", "All dependency rows": "Tous les résultats", "Unresolved includes": "Inclusions non résolues", "Includes": "Inclusions", "Review findings": "Points à examiner", "Preprocessor directives": "Directives du préprocesseur", "Previous dependency rows": "Résultats précédents", "Next dependency rows": "Résultats suivants", "Clear dependency review": "Effacer la revue des dépendances", "No dependency review": "Aucune revue des dépendances", "Open source dependency inspector": "Ouvrir l’inspecteur des dépendances", "Exact supplied-source match": "Correspondance exacte parmi les sources fournies", "Missing selected source": "Source absente de la sélection", "Path capitalization requires review": "Vérifier la casse du chemin", "Ambiguous source capitalization": "Casse des sources ambiguë", "Virtual prefix needs a declared mount": "Le préfixe virtuel nécessite un point de montage déclaré", "Ambiguous virtual mount": "Point de montage virtuel ambigu", "Unsafe include path": "Chemin d’inclusion non sûr", "Computed include requires review": "Inclusion calculée à examiner", "Activation not evaluated": "Activation non évaluée", "Source preview unavailable": "Aperçu source indisponible", "Dependency inspection requires the desktop app": "L’inspection nécessite l’application de bureau", "source files": "fichiers source", "matched includes": "inclusions correspondantes", "unresolved includes": "inclusions non résolues", "Inspecting selected dependencies": "Inspection des dépendances sélectionnées", "Dependency review ready": "Revue des dépendances prête", "Dependency inspection cancelled": "Inspection des dépendances annulée", "Dependency inspection rejected": "Inspection des dépendances refusée", "View source": "Voir la source", "Source dependency inspection": "Inspection des dépendances source", "Assets → Arma 3 migration review → Source dependency inspector: Choose and inspect source files. Select loose SQF/SQM/EXT/HPP/INC/CPP files together, or one source-package JSON containing exactly files and mounts. Loose paths are relative to their common folder; virtual include roots need explicit mounts in a source package. Only selected files are read. Use Unresolved includes, search and paged results, then View source for the captured lines. Exact matches do not prove branch activation, include order or successful compilation. Missing and circular includes remain review candidates. Cancel or a rejected selection retains the previous review; Clear dependency review removes only this session view. Settings provides Open source dependency inspector. This does not edit your plan, execute SQF, connect a bridge or generate Enforce code.": "Assets → Revue de migration Arma 3 → Inspecteur des dépendances source : choisissez les fichiers SQF/SQM/EXT/HPP/INC/CPP ensemble, ou un paquet JSON contenant exactement files et mounts. Les chemins sont relatifs au dossier commun ; les préfixes virtuels nécessitent des montages explicites. Seuls les fichiers choisis sont lus. Filtrez les inclusions non résolues, recherchez et utilisez Voir la source pour consulter les lignes capturées. Une correspondance exacte ne prouve ni activation des branches, ni ordre des inclusions, ni compilation. Les inclusions absentes ou circulaires restent à examiner. Annulation ou refus conserve la revue précédente ; Effacer ne retire que cette vue de session. Les paramètres ouvrent aussi cet inspecteur. Aucun changement du plan, aucune exécution SQF, connexion ou génération Enforce."});

Object.assign(window.PlannerTranslations.de,{"Source dependency inspector": "Quelltext-Abhängigkeitsinspektor", "Select loose source files or one source-package JSON. Only selected sources are inspected; includes are not loaded or executed.": "Quelldateien oder ein Quellpaket-JSON auswählen. Nur gewählte Quellen werden geprüft; Includes werden weder geladen noch ausgeführt.", "Choose and inspect source files": "Quelldateien auswählen und prüfen", "Cancel dependency inspection": "Abhängigkeitsprüfung abbrechen", "Search dependency findings": "Abhängigkeitshinweise durchsuchen", "Dependency rows": "Abhängigkeitszeilen", "All dependency rows": "Alle Abhängigkeitszeilen", "Unresolved includes": "Ungeklärte Includes", "Includes": "Includes", "Review findings": "Prüfhinweise", "Preprocessor directives": "Präprozessoranweisungen", "Previous dependency rows": "Vorherige Abhängigkeitszeilen", "Next dependency rows": "Nächste Abhängigkeitszeilen", "Clear dependency review": "Abhängigkeitsprüfung löschen", "No dependency review": "Keine Abhängigkeitsprüfung", "Open source dependency inspector": "Quelltext-Abhängigkeitsinspektor öffnen", "Exact supplied-source match": "Exakte Übereinstimmung mit gelieferter Quelle", "Missing selected source": "Quelle fehlt in der Auswahl", "Path capitalization requires review": "Gross-/Kleinschreibung des Pfads prüfen", "Ambiguous source capitalization": "Mehrdeutige Gross-/Kleinschreibung der Quellen", "Virtual prefix needs a declared mount": "Virtuelles Präfix benötigt eine deklarierte Zuordnung", "Ambiguous virtual mount": "Mehrdeutige virtuelle Zuordnung", "Unsafe include path": "Unsicherer Include-Pfad", "Computed include requires review": "Berechnetes Include muss geprüft werden", "Activation not evaluated": "Aktivierung nicht ausgewertet", "Source preview unavailable": "Quellvorschau nicht verfügbar", "Dependency inspection requires the desktop app": "Die Prüfung benötigt die Desktop-Anwendung", "source files": "Quelldateien", "matched includes": "zugeordnete Includes", "unresolved includes": "ungeklärte Includes", "Inspecting selected dependencies": "Ausgewählte Abhängigkeiten werden geprüft", "Dependency review ready": "Abhängigkeitsprüfung bereit", "Dependency inspection cancelled": "Abhängigkeitsprüfung abgebrochen", "Dependency inspection rejected": "Abhängigkeitsprüfung abgelehnt", "View source": "Quelle anzeigen", "Source dependency inspection": "Quelltext-Abhängigkeiten prüfen", "Assets → Arma 3 migration review → Source dependency inspector: Choose and inspect source files. Select loose SQF/SQM/EXT/HPP/INC/CPP files together, or one source-package JSON containing exactly files and mounts. Loose paths are relative to their common folder; virtual include roots need explicit mounts in a source package. Only selected files are read. Use Unresolved includes, search and paged results, then View source for the captured lines. Exact matches do not prove branch activation, include order or successful compilation. Missing and circular includes remain review candidates. Cancel or a rejected selection retains the previous review; Clear dependency review removes only this session view. Settings provides Open source dependency inspector. This does not edit your plan, execute SQF, connect a bridge or generate Enforce code.": "Assets → Arma-3-Migrationsprüfung → Quelltext-Abhängigkeitsinspektor: SQF/SQM/EXT/HPP/INC/CPP-Dateien gemeinsam oder ein JSON-Paket mit genau files und mounts auswählen. Pfade beziehen sich auf den gemeinsamen Ordner; virtuelle Präfixe benötigen explizite Zuordnungen. Nur gewählte Dateien werden gelesen. Ungeklärte Includes filtern, suchen und erfasste Zeilen über Quelle anzeigen öffnen. Exakte Treffer beweisen weder Zweigaktivierung, Include-Reihenfolge noch Kompilierbarkeit. Fehlende und kreisförmige Includes bleiben Prüfkandidaten. Abbruch oder Ablehnung erhält die vorherige Prüfung; Löschen entfernt nur diese Sitzungsansicht. Auch über die Einstellungen erreichbar. Keine Planänderung, SQF-Ausführung, Verbindung oder Enforce-Erzeugung."});

